abstract: >-
  We present a comprehensive kill-test of Energy-Flow Cosmology (EFC) against
  ΛCDM across six independent probes spanning galactic to cosmological scales.
  Starting from a single action with two field parameters (K0, m²), EFC
  produces μ = 0.94, η = 1.23, Σ = 1.05 from one mechanism — stiffness and slip
  are not independent. Cobaya minimize runs against Planck 2018 (plik_lite
  TTTEEE + lowl + lensing), BAO, and Pantheon+ consistently return Δχ² ≤ 0 in
  the EFC direction. The same parameter values (K0 ≈ 1.55–1.68, m² ≈
  0.0032–0.0038) reproduce the correct (μ, Σ) independently of starting point.
  EFC cannot be rejected on current data. Full MCMC with Bayes evidence is the
  remaining definitive test.
